      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SUMMER'S LEGACY (3) looked to be in need of her resuming run when peaking late on her run to finish fifth fresh up at Bunbury nearly 2 weeks ago. The powerful Williams stable will have her at peak fitness second up, and she is good enough to take this out. CHOUX SHOE (7) may not win often, but she has been very consistent through the winter months. She carries 2kg less than her last start at Belmont when fifth, and she can figure in the top 3 again with the right run. MY JIMMY (8) snapped a win drought when storming home to score by well over a length at Bunbury nearly a fortnight ago. He only rises 1.5kg for a similar assignment, and he can repeat the dose. PURE OBSESSION (6) did not have all favours off a wide trip at Belmont last start when following on from a gutsy effort for second there before that. With some better luck, he can bounce straight back into the money here.",
